  "raw_meta_yaml": "schema_version: 1\n\ncontext:\n  version: \"1.33.6\"\n\npackage:\n  name: hatchet-sdk\n  version: ${{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  # The PyPI sdist for hatchet-sdk is empty (only contains metadata files like pyproject.toml,\n  # README.md, and PKG-INFO, but no actual Python source code). The wheel contains the full\n  # package code, so we use the wheel directly for installation.\n  - url: https://files.pythonhosted.org/packages/cd/61/fdfb7143e4311b6560edf9edef9cd495a80327d37edadde04fef5954129a/hatchet_sdk-${{ version }}-py3-none-any.whl\n    sha256: deb81fabe417db0bb5dbe9218f737a5a3b7d58eccdfb0e0fddb5fb9730659383\n    file_name: hatchet_sdk-${{ version }}-py3-none-any.whl\n  - url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/hatchet-dev/hatchet/366c79441d9260e63c24727743c3a5271cf239f4/LICENSE\n    sha256: 7388b34bd1ad4b9db3c72dcb73f434ea27c88e5ca8f02a24d4f970c906d79be3\n    file_name: LICENSE\n\nbuild:\n  number: 0\n  noarch: python\n  script:\n    # Use the wheel directly because the sdist is empty of actual code\n    - ${{ PYTHON }} -m pip install hatchet_sdk-${{ version }}-py3-none-any.whl -vv --no-deps --no-build-isolation\n\nrequirements:\n  host:\n    - python ${{ python_min }}.*\n    - pip\n  run:\n    - python >=${{ python_min }}\n    - grpcio >=1.76.0,<2\n    - grpcio-tools >=1.76.0,<2\n    - protobuf >=6.33.5,<7\n    - pydantic >=2.13.3,<3\n    - python-dateutil >=2.9.0.post0,<3\n    - aiohttp >=3.13.5,<4\n    - tenacity >=8.4.1\n    - prometheus_client >=0.25.0\n    - pydantic-settings >=2.14.0,<3\n    - typing-inspection >=0.1.0\n    - urllib3 >=2.7.0,<3\n\ntests:\n  - python:\n      imports:\n        - hatchet_sdk\n        - hatchet_sdk.clients.rest.rest\n        - hatchet_sdk.clients.rest.api\n        - hatchet_sdk.clients.rest.api.workflow_api\n      pip_check: true\n      python_version:\n        - ${{ python_min }}.*\n        - '*'\n\nabout:\n  summary: This is the official Python SDK for Hatchet, a distributed, fault-tolerant task queue. The